   "text": "# Focused Investigation: Post-Restart Health \u2192 Hour-Later Slowdown\n\nThe pattern (healthy at t=0, degraded at t\u224860min) strongly suggests a **time-accumulating resource** rather than a steady-state bottleneck. Split the investigation into three parallel tracks, each with a distinct observable signature.\n\n## Track 1 \u2014 Memory Growth (leak / unbounded accumulation)\n\n**Hypothesis:** RSS or heap grows monotonically until GC pressure, swapping, or OOM-adjacent thrash degrades throughput.\n\n**Observable evidence:**\n- **RSS / heap trend**: `smem`, `ps_mem`, or `/proc/<pid>/status` sampled every 5 min \u2014 look for a monotonic climb that correlates with the slowdown onset, not a plateau.\n- **GC telemetry** (if managed runtime): GC pause time and frequency rising, heap-after-GC rising (true leak) vs. heap-before-GC rising only (allocation churn).\n- **Page faults / swap**: `vmstat 1` \u2014 `si/so` nonzero, or major fault rate climbing; `sar -B` for pgscank/pgsteal.\n- **Allocator stats**: jemalloc/t",
